From: SriAkhilSJ <206201543+SriAkhilSJ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(tools):=20refuse=20the=20foreground=20serve?=
 =?UTF-8?q?r=20that=20ended=20run=207=20=E2=80=94=20`npx=20serve`=20bypass?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ed=20the=20guard?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run 7 proved the search fix (the agent read the literal-match note, switched to `.btn`, and edited the
right files) and then failed to *finish*, which the desktop agent reported honestly: the agent ran
`npx serve . -p 4444` foreground to verify its work, the call blocked, and the 300s harness timeout
ended the turn. Recovery proven, completion not.

The guard that exists for exactly this never saw it. `_foreground_background_guidance` refuses a
foreground command that "would hang until the timeout (it never exits)" and hands back the
`start_terminal` pivot, but its pattern list names `npm|pnpm|yarn|bun … dev|start|serve|watch` —
**`npx` is not in it**. Measured before the fix:

    npx serve . -p 4444    -> passes through (will block)     ← run 7
    npx http-server -p 8080 -> passes through (will block)
    serve -s build          -> passes through (will block)
    php -S localhost:8000   -> passes through (will block)

That is the same class as the search failure: a wrong move that returns *nothing* instead of an error,
leaving the model to discover the cost by burning the turn. Same fix in kind — refuse in zero seconds
and say what to run instead.

Patterns added (marked in the source as crusor additions to hermes' list, with the field evidence):
`npx <server package>` (serve, http-server, live-server, sirv, vite, nodemon, webpack-dev-server,
including `-y`/`--yes` and `@version`), a standalone `serve|http-server|live-server` at the start of a
command or after `|`/`&`/`;`, `php -S`, `flask run`, `manage.py runserver`. `--help`/`--version` stay
exempt, and an over-cap timeout is still *promoted* to a tracked background process rather than
refused, so this only catches the genuinely unbounded foreground server.

False positives were the risk, so the negatives are pinned too: `rg serve src/`, `grep -rn "serve"`
docs/`, `cat serve.log`, `ls dist/serve`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build && ls -la dist` all pass
through, and `npx serve --help` is exempt. Verified to fail without the fix: the new pin goes red when
the additions are removed.

50 passed across the hermes/terminal lanes.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/tests/test_hermes_terminal_guard.py | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/tools/terminal_tools.py             | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/tests/test_hermes_terminal_guard.py b/src/tests/test_hermes_terminal_guard.py
index 255781e1..e46bc954 100644
--- a/src/tests/test_hermes_terminal_guard.py
+++ b/src/tests/test_hermes_terminal_guard.py
@@ -30,6 +30,20 @@ def test_dev_server_commands_refused_with_the_pivot():
         "uvicorn main:app",
         "python -m http.server 8000",
         "docker compose up",
+        # Field 2026-09-26 (preview batch harness, run 7): `npx <pkg>` bypassed the
+        # npm|pnpm|yarn|bun pattern, so this ran foreground to "verify" the agent's edit, blocked
+        # until the harness timeout, and the turn ended with the fix unproven. Refusing it zero
+        # seconds in with the start_terminal pivot is the difference between a proven edit and a
+        # timed-out turn.
+        "npx serve . -p 4444",
+        "npx --yes serve .",
+        "serve -s build",
+        "cd build && serve -s .",
+        "npx http-server -p 8080",
+        "npx live-server",
+        "php -S localhost:8000",
+        "flask run",
+        "python manage.py runserver",
     ):
         msg = _foreground_background_guidance(cmd)
         assert msg is not None, cmd
@@ -45,6 +59,14 @@ def test_bounded_commands_pass_through():
         "node -e console.log(1)",
         "git status",
         "ls .next/BUILD_ID 2>/dev/null || echo no",
+        # The word "serve" is common in ordinary commands; the patterns must name invocations, not
+        # words, or a refusal starts blocking legitimate work.
+        "rg serve src/",
+        'grep -rn "serve" docs/',
+        "cat serve.log",
+        "ls dist/serve",
+        "npx tsc --noEmit",
+        "npm run build && ls -la dist",
     ):
         assert _foreground_background_guidance(cmd) is None, cmd
 
@@ -53,6 +75,7 @@ def test_help_and_version_exempt():
     assert _looks_like_help_or_version_command("npx next dev --help")
     assert _looks_like_help_or_version_command("vite --version")
     assert _foreground_background_guidance("npx next dev --help") is None
+    assert _foreground_background_guidance("npx serve --help") is None
     assert not _looks_like_help_or_version_command("next dev --port 3000")
 
 
diff --git a/src/tools/terminal_tools.py b/src/tools/terminal_tools.py
index 9aad5efa..bf623ab4 100644
--- a/src/tools/terminal_tools.py
+++ b/src/tools/terminal_tools.py
@@ -459,6 +459,18 @@ _LONG_LIVED_FOREGROUND_PATTERNS = tuple(re.compile(p, re.IGNORECASE) for p in (
     r"\buvicorn\b",
     r"\bgunicorn\b",
     r"\bpython(?:3)?\s+-m\s+http\.server\b",
+    # ── crusor additions to hermes' list (2026-09-26), from a measured field failure ──
+    # `npx <pkg>` bypasses the npm|pnpm|yarn|bun pattern above, and that is how run 7 of the preview
+    # harness ended: the agent ran `npx serve . -p 4444` foreground to verify its edit, the call
+    # blocked, and the turn died on the harness timeout with the fix unproven ("recovery proven,
+    # completion not"). These package names bind a port and never exit; `--help`/`--version` remain
+    # exempt above, and a longer timeout is promoted to a tracked background process below rather
+    # than refused, so only the genuinely unbounded foreground server is refused here.
+    r"(?:^|[|&;]\s*)(?:serve|http-server|live-server)\b",
+    r"\bnpx\s+(?:-y\s+|--yes\s+)?(?:serve|http-server|live-server|sirv|vite|nodemon|webpack-dev-server)(?:@[\w.]+)?\b",
+    r"\bphp\s+-S\b",
+    r"\bflask\s+run\b",
+    r"\bmanage\.py\s+runserver\b",
 ))
 
 
